{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "3f6a2f1a-7b3e-4b7e-9e2a-1a2b3c4d5e6f",
        "name": "CAH Private Room + Gameplay",
        "description": "Companion to 'CAH Matchmaking Flow'. That collection only exercises the random matchmaking queue, which auto-creates rooms — it never calls POST /rooms or POST /rooms/join, and never touches the WebSocket gameplay surface at all. This collection covers the private-room path (create by password, join by code) for a controlled 3-player demo, then documents the WebSocket steps to run manually since Postman's native WS requests aren't reliably scriptable into a portable collection JSON.\n\n3 players, not 2: RoomService.start_game hard-requires at least 3 players (rooms.py:391-397, 'Need at least 3 players to start game') — a 2-player room can never leave the lobby.\n\nRun the REST folder top to bottom first (it chains via environment variables, same pattern as the matchmaking collection). Then open three Postman WebSocket requests by hand using the instructions in the 'WebSocket Gameplay' folder description.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "REST Setup",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "01 Register Host",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                        ],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"host_{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"email\": \"host_{{$timestamp}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Pass1234!\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
                            "host": [ "{{baseUrl}}" ],
                            "path": [ "auth", "register" ]
                        }
                    },
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "exec": [
                                    "pm.test(\"Register host returns 201\", function () {",
                                    "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                                    "});",
                                    "const body = pm.response.json();",
                                    "pm.environment.set(\"u1_access\", body.access_token);",
                                    "pm.environment.set(\"u1_refresh\", body.refresh_token);"
                                ],
                                "type": "text/javascript"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "name": "02 Register Guest 1",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [
                            { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
